<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">strength</ansi>

<ansi fg="cyan">Strength</ansi> measures your raw physical power. The stronger you are, the harder
you hit and the more you can carry.

<ansi fg="yellow">Combat</ansi>

* Every strike adds {{ config "GamePlay.Combat.DamageBonusMin" }} damage plus {{ config "GamePlay.Combat.DamagePerStrength" }} per effective Strength,
  with an extra bonus when you are stronger than your opponent: up to
  +{{ config "GamePlay.Combat.DamageEdgeMax" }} at a {{ config "GamePlay.Combat.StatEdgeSpan" }}-point lead, 1/{{ config "GamePlay.Combat.StatEdgeSpan" }} of that per point (<ansi fg="command">help stat-edge</ansi>). The combined
  bonus rounds down and stops at +{{ config "GamePlay.Combat.DamageBonusMax" }} damage, before critical hits and armor.
  Your Strength helps even against an equally strong opponent, but the
  weapon's own dice matter most: a greatsword hits far harder than a dagger.
* Increases the size of your unarmed damage dice when fighting without a weapon.
* With a shield, raises your chance to block a blow, and to slam a blocked
  melee blow back with a shield bash (<ansi fg="command">help shields</ansi>).
* Strength doesn't offset armor bulk: plate slows the strong too
  (<ansi fg="command">help armor</ansi>).

<ansi fg="yellow">Carrying</ansi>

* Adds half a kilogram per point to your share of the company's carrying
  capacity (<ansi fg="command">help cargo</ansi>).
* Adds {{ config "GamePlay.Combat.AgilityStrengthKg" }} kg per point to the load you can fight in before it
  burdens you and cuts your dodge (<ansi fg="command">help burden</ansi>).
</ansi>
